        <div class="pm-contributions">
          <div class="pm-section-title">Greatest Contributions</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Published <em>Micrographia</em> (1665), the first major work on microscopy, coining the term "cell"</li>
            <li>Formulated Hooke's Law (F = kx) -- the foundation of elasticity and material science</li>
            <li>Co-designed the Monument to the Great Fire and helped rebuild London after 1666</li>
            <li>Invented the balance spring for watches, enabling accurate portable timekeeping</li>
            <li>Proposed a wave theory of light and contributed to early ideas about gravity and planetary motion</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-quote">
          <div class="pm-section-title">Key Insight</div>
          <blockquote>Hooke's <em>Micrographia</em> demonstrated that new instruments create new sciences. By looking through a microscope, he saw what no human had ever seen and founded cell biology. The polymath's edge is often instrumental: build the tool, discover the field.</blockquote>
