          <ul>
            <li>Proved lightning is electrical with his famous kite experiment (1752), then invented the lightning rod</li>
            <li>Invented bifocal glasses, the Franklin stove, and the flexible urinary catheter</li>
            <li>Founded the first public lending library, volunteer fire department, and the University of Pennsylvania</li>
            <li>Helped draft and signed the Declaration of Independence, Constitution, and Treaty of Paris</li>
            <li>Mapped the Gulf Stream, advancing oceanography and transatlantic navigation</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-quote">
          <div class="pm-section-title">Key Insight</div>
          <blockquote>"An investment in knowledge pays the best interest." -- Franklin's method was relentlessly practical: every piece of knowledge had to be applicable. He didn't learn for the sake of learning; he learned to solve problems and help his community.</blockquote>
        </div>
